    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the build passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed the `customerCode` format from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` with a per-city sequence.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 `nextCustomerCode` now:\n- Takes `city` in addition to `lastName`.\n- Prepends `CITY3`, the upper-cased first three letters of the city.\n- Computes `NNNN` as a **per-city** sequence (one more than the number of existing owners already in that city, matched case-insensitively and whitespace-trimmed, mirroring the existing `normalizeName` convention), instead of a global owner count.\n- The call site passes `ownerFieldsDto.getCity()`.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 `membershipNumber` already derives from `getCustomerCode()` (`'<customerCode>-M<YY>'`), so it rebuilds on the new format automatically; I only updated its Javadoc example to `'MEL-SMI-0007-M26'`. `membershipTier` doesn't touch the code, so no change needed there.\n\nThe acceptance test (`coreCustomerCodeHasCityPrefix`, asserting `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}`) and the full suite pass \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
